Here's a TypeScript data model for a blog post that balances simplicity with real-world needs.

## Core Types

```typescript
// ---------- Branded ID types ----------
// Prevents accidentally passing an AuthorId where a PostId is expected.
type Brand<T, B extends string> = T & { readonly __brand: B };

export type PostId = Brand<string, "PostId">;
export type AuthorId = Brand<string, "AuthorId">;
export type TagId = Brand<string, "TagId">;

// ISO 8601 timestamp string, e.g. "2024-05-01T12:00:00Z"
export type ISODateString = Brand<string, "ISODateString">;

// ---------- Author ----------
export interface Author {
  id: AuthorId;
  name: string;
  slug: string;          // URL-friendly, e.g. "jane-doe"
  email?: string;
  avatarUrl?: string;
  bio?: string;
}

// Lightweight author reference embedded in posts (avoids duplicating full profile)
export type AuthorSummary = Pick<Author, "id" | "name" | "slug" | "avatarUrl">;

// ---------- Tag ----------
export interface Tag {
  id: TagId;
  name: string;          // Display name, e.g. "TypeScript"
  slug: string;          // URL-friendly, e.g. "typescript"
}

// ---------- Body ----------
// Discriminated union lets you support multiple content formats safely.
export type PostBody =
  | { format: "markdown"; content: string }
  | { format: "html"; content: string }
  | { format: "blocks"; blocks: ContentBlock[] };

export type ContentBlock =
  | { type: "paragraph"; text: string }
  | { type: "heading"; level: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6; text: string }
  | { type: "image"; url: string; alt: string; caption?: string }
  | { type: "code"; language?: string; code: string }
  | { type: "quote"; text: string; attribution?: string }
  | { type: "list"; ordered: boolean; items: string[] };

// ---------- Post status ----------
export type PostStatus =
  | { state: "draft" }
  | { state: "scheduled"; publishAt: ISODateString }
  | { state: "published"; publishedAt: ISODateString }
  | { state: "archived"; archivedAt: ISODateString };

// ---------- Blog Post ----------
export interface BlogPost {
  id: PostId;
  title: string;
  slug: string;
  excerpt?: string;
  author: AuthorSummary;
  tags: Tag[];
  body: PostBody;
  status: PostStatus;
  coverImageUrl?: string;
  createdAt: ISODateString;
  updatedAt: ISODateString;
}
```

## Input / DTO Types

Separating what the client sends from what the server stores keeps server-managed fields (IDs, timestamps) out of user control.

```typescript
// Creating a post: server generates id, timestamps, and resolves author from auth.
export interface CreatePostInput {
  title: string;
  slug?: string;           // Auto-generated from title if omitted
  excerpt?: string;
  tagIds: TagId[];         // Reference existing tags by ID
  body: PostBody;
  coverImageUrl?: string;
}

// Updating: everything optional, but id is required.
export type UpdatePostInput = { id: PostId } & Partial<CreatePostInput>;

// List views usually don't need the full body.
export type BlogPostSummary = Omit<BlogPost, "body">;
```

## Usage Example

```typescript
const post: BlogPost = {
  id: "post_123" as PostId,
  title: "Designing Type-Safe Data Models",
  slug: "designing-type-safe-data-models",
  excerpt: "How to use TypeScript's type system to model your domain.",
  author: {
    id: "auth_42" as AuthorId,
    name: "Jane Doe",
    slug: "jane-doe",
  },
  tags: [
    { id: "tag_1" as TagId, name: "TypeScript", slug: "typescript" },
    { id: "tag_2" as TagId, name: "Architecture", slug: "architecture" },
  ],
  body: {
    format: "markdown",
    content: "# Introduction\n\nTypes are documentation that never lies...",
  },
  status: { state: "published", publishedAt: "2024-05-01T12:00:00Z" as ISODateString },
  createdAt: "2024-04-28T09:00:00Z" as ISODateString,
  updatedAt: "2024-05-01T12:00:00Z" as ISODateString,
};

// Discriminated unions make exhaustive handling easy and safe:
function renderBody(body: PostBody): string {
  switch (body.format) {
    case "markdown": return markdownToHtml(body.content);
    case "html":     return body.content;
    case "blocks":   return body.blocks.map(renderBlock).join("");
  }
}

declare function markdownToHtml(md: string): string;
declare function renderBlock(block: ContentBlock): string;
```

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Branded IDs** | Catches mix-ups like `getPost(authorId)` at compile time. |
| **`AuthorSummary` embedded** | Posts usually need only the name/avatar; the full profile lives elsewhere. |
| **Tags as objects, not strings** | Supports renaming, slugs for URLs, and stable references. Use `string[]` if you want something simpler. |
| **Discriminated union for `body`** | Supports Markdown now and rich blocks later without breaking changes. |
| **Discriminated union for `status`** | Makes invalid states unrepresentable, e.g. a draft can't have a `publishedAt`. |
| **Separate input types** | Clients can't set `id`, `createdAt`, or impersonate another author. |
| **ISO strings for dates** | JSON-serializable. Convert to `Date` at the edges if needed. |

## Minimal Version

If this is more than you need, here's the stripped-down form:

```typescript
