Here's a practical, type-safe data model for a blog post, with explanations of the design choices.

## Core Types

```typescript
// ---------- Branded IDs ----------
// Prevents accidentally passing an AuthorId where a PostId is expected.
type Brand<T, B extends string> = T & { readonly __brand: B };

export type PostId = Brand<string, "PostId">;
export type AuthorId = Brand<string, "AuthorId">;
export type TagId = Brand<string, "TagId">;

// ISO 8601 timestamp string (serializes cleanly to/from JSON)
export type ISODateString = Brand<string, "ISODateString">;

// ---------- Author ----------
export interface Author {
  id: AuthorId;
  name: string;
  slug: string;          // URL-friendly, e.g. "jane-doe"
  email?: string;
  avatarUrl?: string;
  bio?: string;
}

// Lightweight embedded reference, avoids loading full author everywhere
export type AuthorSummary = Pick<Author, "id" | "name" | "slug" | "avatarUrl">;

// ---------- Tag ----------
export interface Tag {
  id: TagId;
  name: string;          // Display name, e.g. "TypeScript"
  slug: string;          // URL-friendly, e.g. "typescript"
}

// ---------- Body ----------
// Discriminated union: supports multiple content formats safely.
export type PostBody =
  | { format: "markdown"; content: string }
  | { format: "html"; content: string }
  | { format: "blocks"; blocks: ContentBlock[] };

export type ContentBlock =
  | { type: "paragraph"; text: string }
  | { type: "heading"; level: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6; text: string }
  | { type: "image"; url: string; alt: string; caption?: string }
  | { type: "code"; language?: string; code: string }
  | { type: "quote"; text: string; attribution?: string }
  | { type: "list"; ordered: boolean; items: string[] };

// ---------- Post Status ----------
// Status determines which fields are present.
export type PostStatus =
  | { status: "draft" }
  | { status: "scheduled"; scheduledFor: ISODateString }
  | { status: "published"; publishedAt: ISODateString }
  | { status: "archived"; publishedAt: ISODateString; archivedAt: ISODateString };

// ---------- Blog Post ----------
export type BlogPost = {
  id: PostId;
  title: string;
  slug: string;
  excerpt?: string;
  author: AuthorSummary;
  tags: Tag[];
  body: PostBody;
  createdAt: ISODateString;
  updatedAt: ISODateString;
} & PostStatus;
```

## Input Types (for create/update operations)

```typescript
// Client sends IDs, server resolves them; server generates id/timestamps.
export interface CreatePostInput {
  title: string;
  slug?: string;          // Auto-generated from title if omitted
  excerpt?: string;
  authorId: AuthorId;
  tagIds: TagId[];
  body: PostBody;
}

export type UpdatePostInput = Partial<Omit<CreatePostInput, "authorId">>;
```

## Usage Example

```typescript
function renderPostDate(post: BlogPost): string {
  switch (post.status) {
    case "draft":
      return "Draft";
    case "scheduled":
      return `Scheduled for ${post.scheduledFor}`;
    case "published":
    case "archived":
      return `Published ${post.publishedAt}`; // TS knows publishedAt exists
  }
}

function getWordCount(body: PostBody): number {
  const count = (s: string) => s.trim().split(/\s+/).filter(Boolean).length;
  switch (body.format) {
    case "markdown":
    case "html":
      return count(body.content);
    case "blocks":
      return body.blocks.reduce((n, b) => {
        if ("text" in b) return n + count(b.text);
        if (b.type === "list") return n + b.items.reduce((m, i) => m + count(i), 0);
        return n;
      }, 0);
  }
}
```

## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Branded IDs** | Compile-time protection against mixing up ID types. |
| **Tags as objects, not strings** | Enables renaming without breaking URLs (via `slug`) and avoids duplicates like "JS" vs "js". |
| **`AuthorSummary` embedded** | Keeps post payloads small; fetch the full `Author` only when needed. |
| **Discriminated union for body** | Lets you support Markdown now and add rich blocks later without breaking changes. |
| **Discriminated union for status** | Makes illegal states unrepresentable, e.g. a draft can't have `publishedAt`. |
| **ISO strings for dates** | Survive JSON serialization; convert to `Date` at the edges. |
| **Separate input types** | Clients can't set server-owned fields like `id` or `createdAt`. |

