## Status-Aware Variant (Stricter)

If you want the type system to guarantee that published posts always have a `publishedAt`, use a discriminated union on status:

```typescript
interface BlogPostBase {
  id: PostId;
  title: string;
  slug: string;
  excerpt?: string;
  body: PostBody;
  authorId: AuthorId;
  tagIds: TagId[];
  createdAt: ISODateString;
  updatedAt: ISODateString;
}

export type BlogPostStrict =
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "draft" })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "scheduled"; scheduledFor: ISODateString })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "published"; publishedAt: ISODateString })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "archived"; publishedAt?: ISODateString; archivedAt: ISODateString });
