## Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Branded IDs** | Prevents passing an `AuthorId` where a `PostId` is expected. They are a compile-time check only, with zero runtime cost. |
| **References vs. embedding** | The stored `BlogPost` holds `authorId`/`tagIds` (normalized), and `BlogPostView` embeds full objects for the client. This avoids stale duplicated data. |
| **Tags as entities** | Tags get their own `id` and `slug` instead of plain `string[]`. This makes renaming, tag pages, and deduplication easy. If you only need simple labels, `tags: string[]` is fine. |
| **Discriminated body** | The format is explicit, so renderers can `switch` exhaustively. Pick one format if you don't need flexibility. |
| **ISO strings over `Date`** | Survives JSON serialization. Convert to `Date` at the edges when needed. |
| **`slug` field** | Gives stable, readable URLs independent of title edits. |

