## Stricter Status Modeling (Optional)

If you want the compiler to enforce that published posts always have a `publishedAt` value, use a discriminated union on `status`:

```typescript
type BlogPostBase = Omit<BlogPost, "status" | "publishedAt">;

export type StrictBlogPost =
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "draft" })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "scheduled"; publishedAt: ISODateString })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "published"; publishedAt: ISODateString })
  | (BlogPostBase & { status: "archived"; publishedAt?: ISODateString });
```

