### Key design decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| **Branded IDs** | Prevents accidentally passing an `AuthorId` where a `PostId` is expected. |
| **Tags as objects, not strings** | Supports renaming tags without breaking references, plus slugs for URLs. Use `string[]` if you want something simpler. |
| **`AuthorSummary` embedded** | Posts usually only need display info, not the full author record. |
| **`PostBody` discriminated union** | Makes the content format explicit and lets you add formats later. |
| **`PostStatus` discriminated union** | Ensures, for example, a `published` post always has `publishedAt`, and a draft can't have one. |
| **Separate input types** | Clients don't supply `id`, `createdAt`, and similar fields. Inputs reference tags and authors by ID. |
| **`BlogPostSummary`** | Keeps list endpoints light by omitting the body. |

