## Design Notes

- **Author and Tag are separate entities** rather than strings, so they can be reused, renamed in one place, and queried (e.g. "all posts by author X").
- **Branded IDs** catch bugs at compile time, like passing an `AuthorId` where a `PostId` is expected.
- **`body` as a discriminated union** lets you add formats later (e.g. rich-text JSON) without breaking existing code. Narrow it with `switch (post.body.format)`.
- **`status` and `publishedAt`** support a draft workflow. If you want to enforce that published posts have a date, you can use a union:
