```ts
type ProductImage = {
  src: string;
  alt: string;
};

type Money = {
  amountMinor: number; // Integer in minor units: 1999 means $19.99 for USD
  currency: string;   // ISO 4217 currency code, e.g. "USD"
};

type ProductPage = {
  name: string;
  price: Money;
  images: ProductImage[];
  description: {
    format: "markdown";
    content: string;
  };
};
```

Markdown supports headings, lists, links, and emphasis without requiring raw HTML. If descriptions come from untrusted sources, disable raw HTML in the Markdown renderer or sanitize the rendered output.

```ts
type ProductPage = {
  name: string;
  price: Price;
  images: [ProductImage, ...ProductImage[]];
  description: FormattedDescription;
};

type Price = {
  /** Amount in the currency's smallest unit: 1999 USD means $19.99. */
  amountInMinorUnits: number;
  /** ISO 4217 currency code, such as "USD" or "EUR". */
  currency: string;
};

type ProductImage = {
  src: string;
  alt: string;
};

type FormattedDescription = {
  format: "markdown";
  content: string;
};
```

The `images` tuple requires at least one image. The description uses Markdown for headings, lists, links, and emphasis.

```ts
type Money = {
  /** Amount in the currency's smallest unit (e.g. 1999 for $19.99 USD). */
  amountMinor: number;
  /** ISO 4217 currency code, e.g. "USD". */
  currency: string;
};

type ProductImage = {
  src: string;
  alt: string;
};

type ProductDescription = {
  format: "markdown";
  content: string;
};

type ProductPage = {
  name: string;
  price: Money;
  /** The first image is the primary product image. */
  images: [ProductImage, ...ProductImage[]];
  description: ProductDescription;
