# Blog Post Data Model

Here's a well-structured TypeScript data model for a blog post. I'll build it up from primitives to the full type, with rationale for each decision.

## Core Types

```typescript
/** Branded ID types prevent mixing up IDs at compile time. */
type Brand<T, B> = T & { readonly __brand: B };

export type PostId = Brand<string, "PostId">;
export type AuthorId = Brand<string, "AuthorId">;
export type TagId = Brand<string, "TagId">;

/** ISO 8601 timestamp, e.g. "2024-06-01T12:00:00Z" */
export type ISODateString = string;

/** URL-safe slug, e.g. "hello-world" */
export type Slug = Brand<string, "Slug">;
```

## Author

```typescript
export interface Author {
  id: AuthorId;
  name: string;
  /** Optional handle, e.g. "@jane" */
  handle?: string;
  avatarUrl?: string;
  bio?: string;
}
```

## Tag

```typescript
export interface Tag {
  id: TagId;
  /** Display name, e.g. "TypeScript" */
  name: string;
  /** URL-safe identifier, e.g. "typescript" */
  slug: Slug;
}
```

## Post Status

```typescript
export type PostStatus =
  | "draft"
  | "published"
  | "archived";
```

## The Blog Post

```typescript
export interface BlogPost {
  id: PostId;
  slug: Slug;

  title: string;
  /** Short summary for previews / SEO. */
  excerpt?: string;
  /** Body content. Format depends on `bodyFormat`. */
  body: string;
  bodyFormat: "markdown" | "html" | "mdx";

  author: Author;
  tags: Tag[];

  status: PostStatus;

  createdAt: ISODateString;
  updatedAt: ISODateString;
  /** Set when status transitions to "published". */
  publishedAt?: ISODateString;

  /** Estimated reading time in minutes. */
  readingTimeMinutes?: number;
  coverImageUrl?: string;
}
```

## Variants (Discriminated Union)

If you want to enforce that published posts *must* have a `publishedAt`, model it as a union:

```typescript
interface PostBase {
  id: PostId;
  slug: Slug;
  title: string;
  excerpt?: string;
  body: string;
  bodyFormat: "markdown" | "html" | "mdx";
  author: Author;
  tags: Tag[];
  createdAt: ISODateString;
  updatedAt: ISODateString;
  coverImageUrl?: string;
}

export interface DraftPost extends PostBase {
  status: "draft";
  publishedAt?: undefined;
}

export interface PublishedPost extends PostBase {
  status: "published";
  publishedAt: ISODateString;
}

export interface ArchivedPost extends PostBase {
  status: "archived";
  publishedAt: ISODateString;
  archivedAt: ISODateString;
}

export type BlogPost = DraftPost | PublishedPost | ArchivedPost;
```

## Design Notes

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| **Branded IDs** | Prevents accidentally passing an `AuthorId` where a `PostId` is expected. |
| **`author` embedded, `tags` as array** | Author is 1:1 and small; tags are many-to-many and often reused. Swap to `authorId` if you fetch authors separately. |
| **`bodyFormat` discriminator** | Lets renderers switch on format without guessing. |
| **`excerpt` optional** | Can be auto-derived from `body` if omitted. |
| **`publishedAt` optional on base, required on `PublishedPost`** | Encodes the invariant "published posts have a publish date" in the type system. |
| **ISO strings over `Date`** | JSON-safe; convert at the boundary. Use `Date` if the model never crosses the wire. |
| **`Slug` branded** | Distinguishes a slug from an arbitrary string. |

## Optional Extensions

If you need them later, these slot in cleanly:

