## Design Notes

| Field | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| **title** | `string`; validate length (e.g., 1–200 chars) at the boundary |
| **author** | Use an object if authors have profiles, avatars, or appear across many posts; a plain `string` is fine for simple cases |
| **tags** | `string[]` for simplicity; `Tag[]` if you need counts, descriptions, or tag pages |
| **body** | Prefer Markdown source + render at read time; use a discriminated union if you support multiple formats |
| **dates** | Store as ISO 8601 strings (`string`) rather than `Date` for JSON-serializability |
| **id** | Use a branded type or `zod`/`uuid` validation to avoid mixing up `PostId` and `TagId` |

**Rule of thumb:** start with Option 1 and refactor to Option 2 when the domain demands it (multiple authors, tag metadata, editorial workflows).

```ts
// A tag attached to a post
export interface Tag {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  slug: string;
}

// An author of a post
