  id: string;
  title: string;
  author: Author;
  tags: Tag[];
  body: string;
  publishedAt?: string; // ISO 8601 date
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

**Notes**

- `author` is a nested object rather than a plain string, so author metadata (bio, avatar) can live alongside the post without a separate lookup table.
- `tags` is an array of `Tag` objects; use `readonly Tag[]` if you want to prevent mutation of the array after creation.
- `body` is plain Markdown or HTML as a string. If you need structured content (headings, images, code blocks), model it as a discriminated union instead:

```ts
