## Design notes

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| `body` is a discriminated union (`format`) | Avoids a "string that might be Markdown or HTML" ambiguity; consumers can `switch (body.format)` and get full type safety. If you only ever have Markdown, simplify to `body: string`. |
| `author` / `tags` are nested objects, not IDs | A blog post is usually rendered as a whole. If your API returns references instead, use `authorId: string` and `tagIds: string[]` and hydrate separately. |
| `status` + `publishedAt` | Distinguishes drafts from live posts and supports scheduled publishing. |
| `slug` separate from `title` | Titles change; URLs usually shouldn't. |
| `createdAt` / `updatedAt` as ISO strings | Serializable across JSON boundaries. Use `Date` only if the model stays in-memory. |

