## Design Notes

| Field | Reasoning |
|---|---|
| `body: string` | Keeps the model storage-agnostic. If you need structure (e.g., blocks), swap it for a discriminated union like `BodyBlock[]`. |
| `tags: Tag[]` | An array (not a set) preserves ordering and serializes cleanly to JSON. Use `readonly Tag[]` if immutability matters. |
| `author: Author` | Embedded object for read-heavy use. If posts reference authors stored elsewhere, use `authorId: AuthorId` instead. |
| Branded IDs | Prevents accidentally passing a `PostId` where an `AuthorId` is expected. |
| ISO date strings | JSON-safe; avoids `Date` serialization pitfalls. Use `Date` if the model stays in-memory only. |
| `status` + separate timestamps | Distinguishes drafts (no `publishedAt`) from published posts and supports scheduled publishing. |

