**Design notes**
- `title`, `category`, `content` are the only required fields; everything else is optional metadata.
- `content` uses `oneOf` so a team can store articles either as raw Markdown (simple, git-friendly) or as structured blocks (better for a CMS/renderer). Pick one convention and enforce it in your ingestion layer.
- `additionalProperties: false` catches typos in field names early.
- `format: "date-time"` and `format: "uri"` are annotations by default — enable format assertion in your validator if you want them enforced.

