## Notes

- **Required vs. optional:** Only `title`, `category`, and `content` are required, so the schema stays easy to satisfy. Everything else is optional metadata.
- **`additionalProperties: false`** catches typos in field names, but remove it if you plan to add fields frequently.
- **`format`** keywords (`date-time`, `email`, `uri`) are annotations by default — enable format assertion in your validator (e.g. `ajv-formats`) if you want them enforced.
- **Category as an enum:** If categories are managed dynamically in a CMS, drop the `enum` and validate against a list fetched at runtime instead.
- **Content validation:** If article bodies have structural requirements (e.g. a minimum number of headings or code blocks), consider modeling `content` as an array of typed blocks (`paragraph`, `heading`, `code`, `image`) rather than a single string.

