### Notes / possible extensions

- **Validation**: pair these types with a runtime schema (Zod, Valibot) so API responses are checked at the boundary — `z.infer<typeof schema>` can generate the same types.
- **Strictness**: enable `"exactOptionalPropertyTypes": true` and `"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true` in `tsconfig.json` for tighter guarantees.
- **i18n**: wrap `name`/`description` in a `Localized<T> = Record<LocaleCode, T>` if the same product is served in multiple languages.
- **A11y**: keep `alt` required on `ProductImage`; for decorative images use `alt: ''` rather than omitting it.

Below is a self-contained set of types. The main design decisions:

- **Money** is stored in **minor units** (integer cents) with an explicit currency — avoids float drift.
- **Images** are a discriminated union so the UI knows which slot an image belongs to.
- **Description** is a **structured rich-text document** (blocks + inline marks) rather than an HTML string, so it can be rendered safely and validated.

```ts
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Primitives                                                          */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

export type Brand<T, B extends string> = T & { readonly __brand: B };

export type ProductId = Brand<string, 'ProductId'>;
export type Sku = Brand<string, 'Sku'>;
export type Slug = Brand<string, 'Slug'>;

/** ISO 4217 code, e.g. "USD", "EUR". */
export type CurrencyCode = 'USD' | 'EUR' | 'GBP' | 'JPY' | 'CAD' | 'AUD' | string;

/**
 * A monetary amount in the currency's *minor unit* (cents, pence, yen).
 * 1999 with "USD" means $19.99.
 */
export interface Money {
  readonly amount: number;
  readonly currency: CurrencyCode;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Images                                                              */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

export type ImageRole = 'hero' | 'gallery' | 'thumbnail' | 'swatch' | 'videoPoster';

export interface ProductImage {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly url: string;
  /** Required for accessibility; falls back to the product name. */
  readonly alt: string;
  readonly role: ImageRole;
  /** Intrinsic dimensions — reserve space to avoid layout shift. */
  readonly width: number;
  readonly height: number;
  /** Optional CDN transformations, e.g. { w: 800, h: 800, fit: 'cover' }. */
  readonly transform?: {
    readonly w?: number;
    readonly h?: number;
    readonly fit?: 'cover' | 'contain' | 'fill';
    readonly dpr?: 1 | 2 | 3;
  };
  /** Marks the image shown in listings / search results. */
  readonly isPrimary?: boolean;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Rich-text description                                               */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

/** Inline formatting marks. `link` carries its own data. */
export type InlineMark =
  | { readonly type: 'bold' }
  | { readonly type: 'italic' }
  | { readonly type: 'underline' }
  | { readonly type: 'strike' }
  | { readonly type: 'code' }
  | { readonly type: 'link'; readonly href: string; readonly title?: string; readonly rel?: string };

export interface TextNode {
  readonly type: 'text';
  readonly text: string;
  readonly marks?: readonly InlineMark[];
}

export interface HardBreakNode {
  readonly type: 'hardBreak';
}

export type InlineNode = TextNode | HardBreakNode;

export interface ListItem {
  readonly content: readonly InlineNode[];
  /** Nested lists. */
  readonly children?: readonly DescriptionBlock[];
}

export interface TableCell {
  readonly content: readonly InlineNode[];
  readonly header?: boolean;
  readonly colspan?: number;
  readonly rowspan?: number;
}

export interface TableRow {
  readonly cells: readonly TableCell[];
}

/**
 * A block-level element of the long description.
 * Discriminated on `type` so renderers can switch exhaustively.
 */
export type DescriptionBlock =
  | { readonly type: 'paragraph'; readonly content: readonly InlineNode[] }
  | {
      readonly type: 'heading';
      readonly level: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6;
      readonly content: readonly InlineNode[];
      /** Anchor id for deep-linking to a section. */
      readonly id?: string;
    }
  | { readonly type: 'bulletList'; readonly items: readonly ListItem[] }
  | { readonly type: 'orderedList'; readonly items: readonly ListItem[]; readonly start?: number }
  | { readonly type: 'blockquote'; readonly content: readonly InlineNode[] }
  | { readonly type: 'callout'; readonly tone: 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'danger'; readonly content: readonly InlineNode[] }
  | { readonly type: 'code'; readonly language?: string; readonly code: string }
  | { readonly type: 'image'; readonly image: ProductImage; readonly caption?: string }
  | { readonly type: 'table'; readonly rows: readonly TableRow[] }
  | { readonly type: 'divider' }
  | { readonly type: 'embed'; readonly provider: 'youtube' | 'vimeo'; readonly url: string; readonly title?: string };

/** The long, formatted product description. */
export interface RichDescription {
  readonly format: 'blocks';
  readonly blocks: readonly DescriptionBlock[];
}

/** Fallback for products with no rich content. */
export interface PlainDescription {
  readonly format: 'plain';
  readonly text: string;
}

export type ProductDescription = RichDescription | PlainDescription;

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Pricing                                                             */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

export interface Price {
  /** The price actually charged. */
  readonly current: Money;
  /** Original / "was" price, when the item is discounted. */
  readonly compareAt?: Money;
  /** Precomputed so the UI never does currency math. */
  readonly discountPercent?: number;
  /** Tax-inclusive vs. tax-exclusive, for display purposes. */
  readonly taxInclusive: boolean;
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Product                                                             */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

export type Availability =
  | { readonly status: 'inStock'; readonly quantity?: number }
  | { readonly status: 'lowStock'; readonly quantity: number; readonly threshold: number }
  | { readonly status: 'outOfStock' }
  | { readonly status: 'preorder'; readonly shipsOn?: string }
  | { readonly status: 'backorder'; readonly leadTimeDays?: number }
  | { readonly status: 'discontinued' };

export interface ProductVariant {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly sku: Sku;
  readonly name: string;
  readonly options: Readonly<Record<string, string>>;
  readonly price: Price;
  readonly image?: ProductImage;
  readonly availability: Availability;
}

export interface Product {
  readonly id: ProductId;
  readonly slug: Slug;
  readonly name: string;
  /** Short marketing line shown under the title. */
  readonly subtitle?: string;
  readonly brand?: string;
  readonly price: Price;
  readonly images: readonly ProductImage[];
  readonly description: ProductDescription;
  readonly variants?: readonly ProductVariant[];
  readonly availability: Availability;
  readonly rating?: {
    readonly average: number;
    readonly count: number;
  };
  readonly attributes?: Readonly<Record<string, string | number | boolean>>;
  readonly tags?: readonly string[];
}

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
/* Page-level wrapper                                                  */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */

export interface Breadcrumb {
  readonly label: string;
  readonly href: string;
}

export interface ProductPage {
  readonly product: Product;
  readonly breadcrumbs: readonly Breadcrumb[];
  readonly seo?: {
    readonly title: string;
    readonly description: string;
    readonly canonicalUrl?: string;
    readonly ogImage?: ProductImage;
  };
  /** Related products for the "you may also like" rail. */
  readonly relatedProducts?: readonly Product[];
}
```

### A few usage notes

**Exhaustive rendering.** Because `DescriptionBlock` is a discriminated union, a renderer can be checked at compile time:

```ts
function renderBlock(block: DescriptionBlock): string {
  switch (block.type) {
    case 'paragraph': return renderInline(block.content);
    case 'heading':   return `<h${block.level}>${renderInline(block.content)}</h${block.level}>`;
    case 'bulletList': return `<ul>${block.items.map(renderListItem).join('')}</ul>`;
    // ...
    default: {
      const _never: never = block; // compile error if a block type is unhandled
      return _never;
    }
  }
}
```

**Narrowing the description.** `description.format` lets you branch without casting:

```ts
const text =
  product.description.format === 'plain'
    ? product.description.text
    : product.description.blocks.map(renderBlock).join('');
```

**If you already have a rich-text editor**, most editors (TipTap/ProseMirror, Slate, Lexical) emit JSON that closely matches the `DescriptionBlock` shape — you can usually map their output onto these types instead of inventing a new format. If you'd rather store Markdown, swap `ProductDescription` for `{ format: 'markdown'; source: string }` and parse at render time.

**Runtime validation.** These types are erased at runtime, so validate API responses at the boundary (e.g. with Zod or Valibot) and derive the types from the schema to keep them in sync.

Below is a complete, production-shaped type module. The main design decisions:

- **Money is stored in minor units** (`amountMinor`) as an integer — never a float.
- **The description is a discriminated union**, so the renderer can exhaustively `switch` on it and the compiler will tell you when a new block type is unhandled.
- **Everything is `readonly`** — product data comes from an API and shouldn't be mutated in place.
- **Dates are ISO 8601 strings**, not `Date`, so the types survive JSON serialization.

