**Design notes**
- `Money.amount` uses minor units to avoid float errors; format at the edge with `Intl.NumberFormat`.
- Rich text is a discriminated union on `type`, so a renderer can `switch` exhaustively and TypeScript will flag missing cases.
- `TextSpan` carries inline formatting (`marks`) and links, while blocks carry structure — mirroring how most CMS rich-text schemas work.
- `ProductImage.alt` is required to enforce accessibility at the type level.

