### Notes / alternatives

- **Money as integer minor units** avoids floating-point rounding errors; format at the UI layer with `Intl.NumberFormat`.
- **If your CMS stores Markdown** instead of structured blocks, simplify to `description: string` (Markdown) and parse with `marked`/`remark` at render time.
- **If you must accept HTML** (e.g. legacy content), use `descriptionHtml: string` but always sanitize with `DOMPurify` before rendering — never `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` on unsanitized input.
- Add runtime validation at the API boundary (e.g. Zod schemas mirroring these types) since TypeScript types vanish at runtime.

Below is a complete, production-oriented type module. The main design decisions:

- **Money is stored as an integer in minor units** (cents) plus a currency code — never a float.
- **The description is a structured document** (discriminated union of blocks), not an HTML blob. This keeps XSS out of the type system, allows rendering to React Native / email / PDF, and makes the shape of "formatting" explicit.
- Everything is `readonly` so a product object can be safely shared/cached.

